    "title": "CA-60 Freeway ramps closed after Monterey Park PD shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matthew Rodriguez ,\n1 hours ago\nPerson hospitalized after Monterey Park police shooting 01:18\nOne person was rushed to the hospital after being shot by the Monterey Park Police Department on Thursday night.\nThe Monterey Park Fire Department said the shooting happened at around 6:35 p.m. on Eastern Avenue near East Los Angeles. The California Highway Patrol closed the 60 Freeway on and off-ramps for investigators. Officers also closed both sides of Eastern Avenue for the investigation.\nThe person's condition was not immediately available.\n1",
    "summary": "Person hospitalized after Monterey Park police shooting 01:18 One person was rushed to the hospital after being shot by the Monterey Park Police Department on Thursday night. The Monterey Park Fire Department said the shooting happened at around 6:35 p.m. on Eastern Avenue near East Los Angeles. The California Highway Patrol closed the 60 Freeway on and off-ramps for investigators. Officers also closed both sides of Eastern Avenue for the investigation. The person's condition was not immediately available.",
